WEBVTT

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:06.150
The Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament Finals.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.950
Satoshi only had Pikachu left,

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:14.370
and Dande had Kyodaimaxed
his supreme partner, Lizardon.

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:19.000
When the Z-Move 10,000,000 Volts
and Kyodai Hellfire collided,

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.290
Galar particles
reacted in abundance.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:24.670
Perhaps sensing
this growing power,

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:28.010
the Legendary Pokémon
Mugendaina appeared.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.980
Mugendaina...

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:42.940
What happened?

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:49.900
Could it be... the one who brought
a vortex of chaos upon the Galar region,

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.280
Mugendaina?!

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:55.160
Grandmother,
everything okay over there?

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:57.910
Mugendaina appeared over
Shoot Stadium!

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:02.250
Yes, we’re fine, Sonia.
What’s happening there?

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:05.920
Galar particles are active to an abnormal degree
in the sky above us.

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:10.430
Then that is likely what Mugendaina
has reacted to.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:17.470
Pikachu!

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.360
Mugendaina... But why?

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:38.360
Stable Galar particles
make for a stable Galar.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:41.740
Mugendaina protected us,
didn’t it?

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:44.000
Keeping our lands peaceful.

00:03:57.050 --> 00:03:59.760
Thanks, Mugendaina.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:01.510
So cool!

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:04.680
Please keep watching over us all.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:08.060
To protect the world from devastation...

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:10.770
To preserve world peace...

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:13.860
Piercing through with the beam
of truth and love...

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:16.940
It’s the lovely, charming Mugendaina...

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:18.910
Just kidding, meow...

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:25.540
Now, let’s collect ourselves
as the match resumes.

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:29.960
Satoshi!
Mugendaina even gave us a little gift!

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:34.170
The Daimax Bands...

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:37.920
Watch this, Mugendaina.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:39.220
Return, Lizardon!

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:43.180
Competitor Dande
recalls Lizardon.

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:45.600
Aceburn, I’m going with you.

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:55.400
Kyodai... max!

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:13.830
This is unprecedented!
Two Kyodaimaxes in a single match!

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.050
Incredible, Big Bro!

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:27.140
Why don’t we try it too, Pikachu?

00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:31.690
I knew you’d say that!

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:36.110
Let’s get huge!

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:39.320
Kyodaimax!

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:57.380
Pikachu’s huge...

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:59.050
Yeah... Amazing...

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:02.050
Competitor Satoshi
also Kyodaimaxes!

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:07.930
What a tumultuous climax
to the Masters Tournament Finals!

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:12.980
Now, let’s do this, Aceburn!
Kyodai Fireball!

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:26.070
He’s not gonna outdo us,
Pikachu!

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:28.240
Kyodai Heavy Thunder!

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:52.730
Kyodai Fireball VS
Kyodai Heavy Thunder!

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:55.810
Both are withstanding
the other’s attack!

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:01.110
And they hit!

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:14.120
Pikachu!

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:17.040
Aceburn!

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:21.000
The intense power forced them both
back to normal size!

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:31.010
Aceburn is unable to battle!

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:36.270
Pikachu wins the
Kyodaimax showdown!

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:38.350
All right! We did it, Pikachu!

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:42.020
He did it!

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:47.910
Pi-ka-chu! Pi-ka-chu! Pi-ka—!

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:49.740
Big Bro...

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:55.540
Return, Aceburn.

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:01.790
Your Kyodaimax was incredible.

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:06.010
Satoshi! Our final battle...

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:07.800
...really did come down to these two.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:10.550
Yeah! A partner showdown!

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:12.760
Come out, Lizardon!

00:08:20.230 --> 00:08:23.110
The Masters Tournament Finals!

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:28.490
Competitors Dande and Satoshi
are both down to their last Pokémon...

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:32.580
Lizardon and Pikachu!

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:36.290
You’ve done well,
pushing me this far.

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:40.460
You’ve made me grow
even stronger.

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:46.210
Let’s burn brighter and brighter,
until our very last blow!

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:56.720
We’ve kept growing stronger
because of you and your team.

00:08:57.850 --> 00:09:01.940
This battle...
Everything since me and Pikachu met...

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:04.940
All our adventures
come together in this battle!

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:09.150
Which is why...
We’re gonna win!

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:14.740
Go! Lightning Speed!

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:17.830
Primal Power!

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:29.220
Pikachu strikes first!

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:31.550
Iron Tail!

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:35.180
Blow him away!

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:44.560
Pikachu!

00:09:47.070 --> 00:09:48.190
Air Slash!

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:58.540
Great Blaze!

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:02.790
Electroweb!

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:09.880
Run for it, Pikachu!

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:17.640
Pikachu narrowly dodges
the Great Blaze!

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:19.720
100,000 Volts!

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:22.940
Great Blaze!

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:30.570
You okay?

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:33.150
You’re still good to go, yeah?

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:49.590
Iron Tail!

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:54.590
Lizardon, take the hit!

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:02.680
Dragon Pulse!

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:18.280
We’re not done.
We’re just getting <i>started!</i>

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:26.460
This is the best!
Satoshi! Pikachu!

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:29.250
Let’s raise our power higher,
Lizardon!

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:40.850
Win it! Big Bro! Lizardon!

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:01.990
Pikachu! Use Lightning Speed!

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:09.710
What?! I didn’t see a thing!

00:12:10.170 --> 00:12:12.290
Primal Power!

00:12:27.270 --> 00:12:28.640
Air Slash!

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:34.530
Iron Tail!

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:43.200
Wow...

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:52.130
Great Blaze!

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:55.550
100,000 Volts!

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:01.340
Whoa! The 100,000 Volts
didn’t make it!

00:13:01.340 --> 00:13:03.550
It got engulfed by
the Great Blaze!

00:13:16.780 --> 00:13:17.820
Pikachu!

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:12.540
Pikachu!

00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:19.300
It’s so cute! It’s the best one!

00:14:19.300 --> 00:14:21.340
Pikachu, nice to meet you.

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:29.780
That’s right, Pikachu!
Everyone’s at our side!

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:58.020
Be it fire, water, grass, or forests,

00:15:54.310 --> 00:15:56.850
Good job, Pikachu!
You stood back up!

00:15:57.270 --> 00:15:59.980
Now <i>there’s</i> the Satoshi and Pikachu
I was waiting for!

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:01.900
the ground, the clouds, or under that girl’s skirt (Eek!)

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:01.900
Pikachu!

00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:05.820
It’s really, really, really, really hard to handle,

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:05.190
We’re gonna bet it all
on this attack!

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:13.990
but I’m gonna get them all! I’m gonna get Pokémon!

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:09.620
Lizardon!

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:13.990
It’s Champion time!

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:17.330
Masara Town, I bid you goodbye

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:21.750
I’m going on a journey with this little guy (Pikachu!)

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:21.750
100,000 Volts!

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:25.800
I’ll win each battle with the moves I’ve mastered,

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:29.590
then head to the next town and make friends along the way!

00:16:27.470 --> 00:16:29.890
Great Blaze!

00:16:29.590 --> 00:16:33.600
There’s no way to know for sure

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:37.560
if things will always work out (Got that right!)

00:16:36.350 --> 00:16:38.230
Go!

00:16:37.560 --> 00:16:48.280
But with my companions by my side, we’ll live life to the fullest!

00:17:02.420 --> 00:17:05.000
Pikachu! You okay?

00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:12.090
You were awesome
out there, Pikachu.

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:18.060
Your last attack
left me electrified!

00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:55.010
Lizardon is unable to battle!

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:58.520
As such, the winner is
Competitor Satoshi!

00:17:58.520 --> 00:18:03.600
It’s over!
A new Champion is born today!

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:09.900
Hailing from Masara Town in Kanto,
Competitor Satoshi!

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:16.410
Pikachu!

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:30.550
Thank you so much!
We beat Mr. Dande thanks to you!

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:42.560
Ooh, I see Pikachu’s all perked up.

00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:43.730
Mr. Dande!

00:18:46.860 --> 00:18:49.820
That was a great battle.
I had fun!

00:18:49.820 --> 00:18:51.990
I had fun, too!

00:18:51.990 --> 00:18:56.240
It reminded me of my first-ever
Pokémon battle.

00:19:01.040 --> 00:19:02.500
It was fun...

00:19:10.550 --> 00:19:11.960
It was frustrating...

00:19:15.010 --> 00:19:19.140
And it made me think,
“So this is a real Pokémon battle.”

00:19:19.140 --> 00:19:20.220
Yeah.

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:24.600
From today,
I’m just another challenger.

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:27.850
I’ll have lots of battles
and get even stronger!

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:30.650
I wanna battle lots more, too!

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:35.530
Let’s battle again sometime.

00:19:37.950 --> 00:19:40.620
Yeah. For sure!

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:46.210
Satoshi! It’s almost time
for the award ceremony!

00:19:46.210 --> 00:19:48.040
Um... That goes for
you too, Mr. Dande.

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:56.010
Gathering Champions from various regions,
giving us the greatest of spectacles...

00:19:56.010 --> 00:20:00.550
The Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament.

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:07.520
Now, Competitor Dande presents the trophy
to our new Champion, Competitor Satoshi!

00:20:24.870 --> 00:20:29.210
Celebrating with
A display of fireworks
Lovely it is

00:20:29.210 --> 00:20:34.130
All of the allies
Who waited dearly for this
Have a mother’s thanks

00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:42.260
All of a sudden...
I’m in the mood for a battle now, too.

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:45.020
How about one, right now?

00:20:47.020 --> 00:20:49.900
Satoshi! Congrats!

00:20:49.900 --> 00:20:51.480
Congrats!

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:54.610
My... Now that’s our Pikachu...

00:20:54.610 --> 00:20:57.610
I’m full of emotions
right now, meow...

00:20:57.610 --> 00:21:00.410
But I feel like we’re
forgetting something...

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:11.080
Satoshi finally took down the undefeated Dande,
and was crowned as the supreme battler.

00:21:11.710 --> 00:21:16.420
The Pokémon World Championships, weaver of many a grand battle...

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:18.220
...have concluded!

00:21:29.310 --> 00:21:37.690
Incoming call from Go.
Incoming call from Go.

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:40.990
Pikachu!
It’s gotta be about Mew!

00:21:42.410 --> 00:21:44.570
Hello? Go?

00:23:07.240 --> 00:23:09.660
Now, off to the next adventure!

00:23:09.660 --> 00:23:10.950
Go!

00:23:11.870 --> 00:23:17.040
We Chasers will land on Faraway Island
and begin our search for Mew.

00:23:18.290 --> 00:23:19.630
Our transmitters...

00:23:19.630 --> 00:23:20.960
Our Smartphone Rotoms...

00:23:21.340 --> 00:23:23.090
Even our Monster Balls?!

00:23:23.090 --> 00:23:24.930
None of our devices
are working?!

00:23:24.930 --> 00:23:28.800
We’ll try a different route
to the center!

00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:30.930
We’ll keep heading up!

00:23:30.930 --> 00:23:32.850
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:32.850 --> 00:23:34.430
Project Mew
